# REGRESSION PIN (graduated from known_gaps/, `todo/t0936`).
#
# `.clone()` on a value-form `Callable` used to lower to `Constant::Unit`, and
# the emitted C then memcpy'd sizeof(GorgetClosure) out of that unit slot —
# SIGSEGV (rc 139) on BOTH backends, with `gg check` clean.
#
# ROOT CAUSE (fire count 0 at the clone arm, 1 after the fix):
# `infer_type_name_from_operand_full` (src/ir/lowering/exprs/methods.rs)
# returned None for a `GirType::FnPtr` receiver, so the whole block gated by
# `if let Some(type_name)` — which contains the `.clone()` arm — was skipped.
# That function already documented this exact class for a previously-fixed
# sibling (the `I64_TYPE` arm). `clone_fn_for_ptr` (context.rs) was
# `GirType::Named`-only and is the necessary second arm: with the dispatch-name
# arm alone the build fails on `incompatible type for argument 1 of
# 'gorget_closure_clone_to_owned'`.
#
# NOT a carve-out violation: Callable is single-owner WITH a real clone path
# (`decisions.md:114` / `:525`, `builtins.rs:1109`), pinned green by
# tests/fixtures/security/attack_91_callable_clone_outlives_source.gg.
#
# The WIDE net for this axis is tests/fixtures/callable_clone_value_form_axis.gg.
void main():
    Callable[int(int)] h = (int x): x + 1
    Callable[int(int)] g = h.clone()
    print(g(1))
